1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,750
No worries, y'all.
别担心，各位。

2
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:06,110
I'm having that fun feeling.
我现在特别开心。

3
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:10,500
Go, Norway!
加油，挪威！

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,380
Christopher Nolan's The Odyssey, is a story about the journeys that shape us.
克里斯托弗·诺兰的《奥德赛》，讲述的是那些塑造我们的旅程。

5
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:18,820
For Erling Haaland, that journey is just beginning.
而对埃尔林·哈兰德来说，这段旅程才刚刚开始。

6
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:21,550
A World Cup decades in the making.
一届筹备了数十年的世界杯。

7
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:31,780
A moment his father once experienced years ago, and a nation now living it alongside him.
这一刻，他的父亲多年前曾亲历，如今整个国家正与他一同经历。

8
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:33,310
The journey continues.
旅程仍在继续。

9
00:00:33,310 --> 00:00:36,190
Like Odysseus setting sail for the unknown.
如同奥德修斯扬帆驶向未知。

10
00:00:36,190 --> 00:00:40,350
Erling and Team Norway begin the next stage of their adventure.
埃尔林与挪威队，踏上冒险的下一段征程。

11
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:44,910
But before the training begins, there is still time for familiar routines.
但在训练开始之前，还有时间做做熟悉的日常。

12
00:00:44,910 --> 00:00:49,070
A flight, a few laughs, and a lot of time gaming.
一趟飞行，几声欢笑，还有大把时间打游戏。

13
00:00:49,070 --> 00:00:53,070
It was of course special to meet up with team and to travel.
能和队伍会合、一起出行，当然很特别。

14
00:00:53,070 --> 00:00:55,430
This is something we've been working for years, you know?
这是我们为之努力了好多年的事，你懂吗？

15
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,520
So, normally on long flights, you sleep.
通常长途飞行，你会睡觉。

16
00:00:57,520 --> 00:01:04,180
I didn't sleep a second, you know, because you're excited, and you're looking forward to it.
可我一秒都没睡，因为太兴奋了，太期待了。

17
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:09,150
Lovely.
太好了。

18
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:10,870
Facilities here are really nice.
这里的设施真的很棒。

19
00:01:10,870 --> 00:01:16,030
The hotel is nice, and the weather is good, so we've been relaxing today, playing a little bit of golf.
酒店不错，天气也好，所以今天我们一直在放松，打了会儿高尔夫。

20
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:18,820
Got a little bit sunburned, of course, as always.
当然，照例又晒伤了一点。

21
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:20,400
You've been in the gym, or what?
你去健身房了，是吧？

22
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:20,820
Yes.
是的。

23
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:22,070
And I'll be in the gym.
我还会继续去健身房。

24
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:22,560
Congrats.
恭喜啊。

25
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:23,920
I've been in champ outside.
我在外面可一直是冠军。

26
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:24,560
Congrats.
恭喜。

27
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,030
Carrying Martine on my back.
我可是一路背着马丁带飞。

28
00:01:26,030 --> 00:01:28,350
He bought a new golf set for me, by the way.
对了，他给我买了一套新的高尔夫球杆。

29
00:01:28,350 --> 00:01:30,070
Yeah, I'm sorting out.
对，我在张罗呢。

30
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:34,510
First time in life, I've sorted him out, and he's not sorted me out.
这辈子头一回，是我搞定他，而不是他搞定我。

31
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:39,630
Thousands of miles from home, Erling finds himself interacting with a different kind of fan.
远离家乡数千英里，埃尔林遇到了另一类球迷。

32
00:01:39,630 --> 00:01:43,790
Some know exactly who he is, others are meeting him for the first time.
有些人完全知道他是谁，有些人则是第一次见到他。

33
00:01:43,790 --> 00:01:47,870
But as Norway prepares for battle, that won't be the case for long.
但随着挪威备战，这种情况不会持续太久。

34
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:51,070
Are y'all on the Norwegian soccer team?
你们都是挪威足球队的吗？

35
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:52,510
Uh, no, not me.
呃，不，我不是。

36
00:01:52,510 --> 00:01:54,590
No, not you?
不，你不是？

37
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:55,150
Really?
真的吗？

38
00:01:55,150 --> 00:01:57,460
I'm the social media guy.
我是搞社交媒体的。

39
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,480
Y'all are lying to me.
你们在骗我。

40
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,550
Somebody just told me that one of you is like, the biggest soccer player in the world.
有人刚跟我说，你们当中有个是全世界最大牌的球员。

41
00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:02,640
You're looking at him.
他就在你眼前。

42
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:05,200
So take photo of both of us, and you show it to him.
那你给我俩拍张合照，再拿给他看。

43
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,670
And say which one?
然后问他是哪一个？

44
00:02:06,670 --> 00:02:07,790
No worries, y'all.
别担心，各位。

45
00:02:07,790 --> 00:02:09,870
That's your American Southern accent.
这就是你的美国南方口音。

46
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:11,140
There it is, doll.
这就对了，亲爱的。

47
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:14,420
Not the doll.
别叫我“亲爱的”。

48
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:16,660
Greensboro is not a huge city.
格林斯伯勒不是个大城市。

49
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:18,400
We can go anywhere in 20 minutes.
去哪儿都只要 20 分钟。

50
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,680
It's easy for them to get around.
他们出行很方便。

51
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:22,660
The roads aren't crowded, so it's kind of a perfect place for them.
路上不堵车，对他们来说算是个完美的地方。

52
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:28,800
It's really cool to have a world class World Cup international team here with these elite players.
能有这样一支世界级的世界杯球队、带着这些顶尖球员来到这里，真的很酷。

53
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:32,500
Brings a lot of notoriety to Greensboro.
给格林斯伯勒带来了很高的知名度。

54
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:35,870
It's back to work with the start of training before game one.
随着首场比赛前训练的开始，一切重回正轨。

55
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:38,420
The goal was always qualification.
目标始终是晋级正赛。

56
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:43,700
Now, it's Team Norway's chance to prove they belong here right on the world's biggest stage.
如今，挪威队有机会在世界最大的舞台上证明自己配得上这里。

57
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:52,340
You can feel the excitement, even me, myself, got so much energy, and I'm so ready to just finally play the World Cup.
你能感受到那种兴奋，连我自己都浑身是劲，终于能踢世界杯了，我已经准备好了。

58
00:02:52,340 --> 00:03:01,620
We have to be confident, and yeah, with Erling up front with Martin behind him with, we've got good chances.
我们必须有信心，有埃尔林顶在前面、马丁在他身后，我们机会很大。

59
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:06,150
Now it's all about training, getting ready for the game, because now I had a little bit off.
现在重点全在训练、备战上，因为之前我休息了一阵。

60
00:03:06,150 --> 00:03:10,340
I've been relaxing a little bit, playing a bit of golf, been with my family,
我放松了一下，打了打高尔夫，陪了陪家人，

61
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:15,380
with my friends, my form and my shape is there, so it's just about getting back in the rhythm.
也见了朋友，我的状态和身体都在，所以现在只是要找回节奏。

62
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:18,340
Don't try to do anything different now, just because it's World Cup.
别因为这是世界杯，就刻意去做什么不一样的事。

63
00:03:18,340 --> 00:03:20,750
I try not to think too much about the games.
我尽量不去想太多比赛的事。

64
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:23,380
Overthink things, I think you start stressing a little bit,
想太多，就会开始有点紧张，

65
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:29,360
so for me, even now, it's the most difficult thing to think of the games, which I do.
所以对我来说，即便现在，最难的就是去想比赛——而我确实会想。

66
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:32,180
I think of the first game, how it will be and all of that,
我会想首场比赛，会是什么样，诸如此类，

67
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:40,590
but you need to kind of put your feelings aside a bit in big occasions and just do what you do the best,
但在大场面里，你得把情绪稍微放到一边，做你最擅长的事，

68
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:45,940
just focus on doing your job.
只管专注做好自己的本职。

69
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:49,540
The confidence is there, without a doubt, we know what to do as a team.
信心毫无疑问是有的，作为一支球队，我们知道该怎么做。

70
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:52,750
I mean, in the qualification games, we won eight out of eight.
我是说，预选赛里我们八战全胜。

71
00:03:52,750 --> 00:03:55,940
Honestly, no matter how it will go, it will be a successful thing.
老实说，不管结果如何，这都已经算成功了。

72
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:59,460
I know it sounds wrong, but we qualified for the first time in 28 years.
我知道这话听着别扭，但我们是 28 年来头一次晋级。

73
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:01,780
Of course, I want to go through.
当然，我想出线。

74
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:06,590
I want to go far, all of these kind of things, but in the end,
我想走得更远，诸如此类，但说到底，

75
00:04:06,590 --> 00:04:08,560
let's just go through and then be happy.
先出线，然后开开心心的。

76
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,200
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
哦，对，对，对。

77
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:14,900
Come on!
来吧！

78
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:15,840
Let's go, Norway!
加油，挪威！

79
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:15,940
Let's go, Norway!
加油，挪威！

80
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:22,160
When I saw him come out here on the pitch, I said, "Oh my God, he's a Viking."
当我看到他走上球场，我就说：“我的天，他就是个维京人。”

81
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:24,020
Like, I got it.
那一刻我懂了。

82
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:31,380
We have been transported back to the 16 or 1700s, and there's a live Viking in front of us.
仿佛我们穿越回了十六、十七世纪，眼前活生生站着一个维京人。

83
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:35,550
You know, it's a smaller stadium, so we can seat 3,500.
你知道，这是个较小的球场，只能容纳 3500 人。

84
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:40,990
We had requests for over 20,000 seats.
可我们收到了超过两万个座位的需求。

85
00:04:40,990 --> 00:04:42,480
There is so much energy.
气氛太火热了。

86
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:48,820
There's so much buzz around soccer and the FIFA World Cup.
围绕足球和国际足联世界杯，到处都是热议。

87
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:51,620
Day by day, the group grows stronger.
一天天过去，这个集体愈发强大。

88
00:04:51,620 --> 00:05:00,260
New surroundings, new supporters, and another opportunity for Norway to come together before the tournament begins.
新的环境，新的支持者，也是挪威在大赛开始前再次凝聚的又一次机会。

89
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:06,260
The pressure never completely disappears, which is why preparation also means stepping away from it.
压力从未完全消失，所以备战也意味着适时抽离。

90
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:09,460
Time to reset, time to switch off.
是时候重置自己，是时候放空一下。

91
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:12,900
Tonight, that means trading football for ice hockey.
今晚，这意味着把足球暂时换成冰球。

92
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:20,820
Going to the Carolina Hurricanes, against Las Vegas Knights, Stanley Cup final, it's the fifth game, it's 2-2.
去看卡罗来纳飓风队对阵拉斯维加斯骑士队，斯坦利杯总决赛第五场，目前 2 比 2。

93
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:23,380
So it's gonna be one hell of a game.
所以这肯定是场精彩绝伦的比赛。

94
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:24,900
I'm sure about that.
这点我很确定。

95
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:28,720
I think it's good for us to spend some time out of the hotel as well,
我觉得我们出去走走、离开酒店一阵也挺好，

96
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:32,820
and do something else, 'cause you go a bit mad at the hotel.
做点别的事，因为老待在酒店会有点闷得发慌。

97
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:34,950
I don't know if I've ever been to a hockey game live.
我都不记得自己有没有现场看过冰球了。

98
00:05:34,950 --> 00:05:37,380
I'm lucky.
我很幸运。

99
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:39,360
I'll be smart.
我会机灵点的。

100
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:45,550
I'm starting to feel it now, are you?
我开始有感觉了，你呢？

101
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:47,870
This is incredible.
这太不可思议了。

102
00:05:47,870 --> 00:05:53,460
Wait and see when we go on the big screen there.
等着瞧，等我们上了那边的大屏幕。

103
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:54,000
Perfect.
完美。

104
00:05:54,000 --> 00:06:04,070
I've been eating healthy since I came to the U.S, but now I enjoy some American food, and be in the hockey vibe.
来美国以后我一直吃得很健康，但现在我也享受下美式食物，融入冰球的氛围。

105
00:06:04,070 --> 00:06:05,360
They have so much, like, pride for the country.
他们对自己的国家有着满满的自豪感。

106
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:05,920
They love their country so much.
他们太爱自己的国家了。

107
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:06,560
It's everything about it.
方方面面都是如此。

108
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,790
National anthem was incredible.
国歌环节太震撼了。

109
00:06:07,790 --> 00:06:08,870
Amazing.
了不起。

110
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:09,750
I had goosebumps all over.
我全身都起了鸡皮疙瘩。

111
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:12,160
Play for Manchester United is apparently the best soccer player in the world right now.
他效力于曼联，据说是当今世界上最强的球员。

112
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:12,800
I never, ever expected this.
我从没想过会这样。

113
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,750
Atmosphere is unreal.
气氛简直不真实。

114
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:36,350
Good to get the head a bit away from football, think about something else.
能让脑子暂时离开足球、想想别的，挺好。

115
00:06:36,350 --> 00:06:44,400
Just enjoying the ice hockey, so it's good.
就是单纯享受冰球，挺好的。

116
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:45,040
We're enjoying it.
我们看得很尽兴。

117
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:55,550
You know, we're not here for the ice hockey.
你知道，我们来这儿可不是为了冰球。

118
00:06:55,550 --> 00:06:56,560
Of course, it's nice.
当然，这很不错。

119
00:06:56,560 --> 00:07:12,350
But in the end, we're here to perform for Norway.
但归根结底，我们来这儿是为挪威而战。

120
00:07:12,350 --> 00:07:17,870
We have to lock in in a few days before it get real.
再过几天就要动真格了，我们必须全力进入状态。

121
00:07:17,870 --> 00:07:21,230
The atmosphere, the energy, the passion of the crowd.
现场的气氛、能量，还有观众的激情。

122
00:07:21,230 --> 00:07:26,750
It's a reminder that no matter the sport, great moments have a way of bringing people together.
它提醒着我们：无论哪项运动，伟大的时刻总能把人们凝聚在一起。

123
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:35,310
Best live experience ever.
有史以来最棒的现场体验。

124
00:07:35,310 --> 00:07:42,110
Boston is a long way from home, but for Erling's fans, who've crossed oceans to be a part of the experience.
波士顿离家乡很远，但对那些漂洋过海、只为亲身参与的埃尔林的球迷而言——

125
00:07:42,110 --> 00:07:45,550
The journey is part of the experience.
旅途本身，也是体验的一部分。

126
00:07:45,550 --> 00:07:47,700
Haaland, Haaland, Haaland.
哈兰德，哈兰德，哈兰德。

127
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:52,990
28 years ago, Alf-Inge Holland walked onto football's biggest stage as a player.
28 年前，阿尔夫-因格·哈兰德以球员身份踏上足球最大的舞台。

128
00:07:52,990 --> 00:07:56,020
Today, he returns to it as a father.
今天，他以父亲的身份重返这里。

129
00:07:56,020 --> 00:08:03,380
Well, just in case things goes wrong tonight, at least we can have a cigar.
好吧，万一今晚出了岔子，至少我们还能抽根雪茄。

130
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:08,260
He's played a lot of big games, but we can all feel it's a little bit special today.
他踢过很多大赛，但我们都能感觉到，今天有些特别。

131
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:11,550
Representing a country, being in the World Cup.
代表一个国家，征战世界杯。

132
00:08:11,550 --> 00:08:17,430
I probably will get more nervous than I've ever been to a game watching him play.
看他踢球，我大概会比以往任何一场都更紧张。

133
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:20,350
So I'm still looking forward to that.
但我依然很期待。

134
00:08:20,350 --> 00:08:23,700
I always tell them, you never know how it's gonna go,
我总是告诉他们，你永远不知道结果会怎样，

135
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:28,020
but the thing you can do every time is to give 100%.
但你每次都能做到的，就是拿出百分之百。

136
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:32,670
I'm very proud of all my kids, but obviously, this is a little bit special.
我为我所有的孩子骄傲，但显然，这一次有点特别。

137
00:08:32,670 --> 00:08:34,560
I haven't played in the World Cup myself.
我自己没踢过世界杯。

138
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:39,440
It's a little bit special that his first World Cup, hopefully, it will be a couple more,
他的第一届世界杯，这本身就有点特别，但愿后面还会有好几届，

139
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:44,110
but to also play here, it's special, and then, obviously, I'm proud, yeah.
而且还能在这里出战，很特别，我当然，很骄傲，是的。

140
00:08:44,110 --> 00:09:06,910
As Norway prepares for their first match, fans from across the world gather in anticipation right before kickoff.
随着挪威备战首场比赛，开球前，来自世界各地的球迷满怀期待地聚集在一起。

141
00:09:06,910 --> 00:09:30,990
Iran, Iran.
伊朗，伊朗。

142
00:09:30,990 --> 00:09:33,750
Go on, Norway!
上啊，挪威！

143
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:34,240
Go, Norway!
加油，挪威！

144
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:34,720
We love Norway!
我们爱挪威！

145
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,440
What's up, Norway?
怎么样，挪威？

146
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,710
When he scored, it was, uh, completely chaos in the stands.
他进球的时候，看台上简直乱成一团。

147
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:38,480
I can't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

148
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,710
He has two goals.
他梅开二度。

149
00:09:39,710 --> 00:09:43,390
4-1 winner, our first game in the World Cup in 28 years.
4 比 1 获胜，这是我们 28 年来的第一场世界杯比赛。

150
00:09:43,390 --> 00:09:45,550
I can't believe it.
我真不敢相信。

151
00:09:45,550 --> 00:09:49,030
Norway, Norway, Norway, Norway.
挪威，挪威，挪威，挪威。

152
00:09:49,030 --> 00:09:50,800
World Cup debut, we win.
世界杯首秀，我们赢了。

153
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,030
I scored two goals.
我进了两球。

154
00:09:52,030 --> 00:09:53,310
Fans were amazing.
球迷太棒了。

155
00:09:53,310 --> 00:09:56,750
Good game as well, so, uh, it was good.
比赛也踢得不错，所以，挺好的。

156
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:59,630
I didn't know Mbappe scored two goals.
我都不知道姆巴佩进了两球。

157
00:09:59,630 --> 00:10:01,790
The second goal he scored was amazing, by the way.
顺便说，他进的第二个球太精彩了。

158
00:10:01,790 --> 00:10:04,430
Messi scored a hat trick in the night.
梅西当晚上演帽子戏法。

159
00:10:04,430 --> 00:10:09,070
We were watching the game on the bus and on the plane.
我们在大巴上、飞机上都在看比赛。

160
00:10:09,070 --> 00:10:11,950
It was incredible.
太不可思议了。

161
00:10:11,950 --> 00:10:13,950
Messi scored a hat trick.
梅西上演了帽子戏法。

162
00:10:13,950 --> 00:10:17,230
Then the day after, I think, Kane scored two as well.
然后第二天，我记得凯恩也进了两球。

163
00:10:17,230 --> 00:10:25,510
So, there's been a lot of goals in this World Cup, and, I mean, the best goal scorers are playing in this tournament,
所以这届世界杯进球如潮，我是说，最会进球的那些人都在这届赛事里，

164
00:10:25,510 --> 00:10:28,990
so it's gonna be, it's gonna be scoring a lot of goals.
所以肯定会，肯定会有很多进球。

165
00:10:28,990 --> 00:10:31,710
I'm sure of that.
这点我很确定。

166
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:32,390
I don't know.
我也说不好。

167
00:10:32,390 --> 00:10:36,830
I think, yeah, I think it motivates you, but I think you're motivated anyways.
我觉得，嗯，这确实会激励你，但其实你本来就有动力。

168
00:10:36,830 --> 00:10:39,230
To score goals and to win games.
去进球，去赢球。

169
00:10:39,230 --> 00:10:43,750
Because for me, personally, I don't, of course, you thrive on scoring goals,
因为对我个人而言，当然，进球会让你越战越勇，

170
00:10:43,750 --> 00:10:50,320
but you want the team to win, so it doesn't really, it doesn't really matter who scores as long as you win.
但你更想让球队获胜，所以谁进球其实并不重要，只要能赢就行。

171
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,590
But of course, I'm the striker for Norway.
当然，我是挪威的前锋。

172
00:10:52,590 --> 00:10:54,510
You want to score goals.
你会想进球。

173
00:10:54,510 --> 00:10:57,150
You have to score goals, that's the part of your job.
你必须进球，这是你工作的一部分。

174
00:10:57,150 --> 00:11:03,390
But it probably motivates you a little bit, but in the end, what motivates you is,
进球或许确实会激励你一点，但归根结底，真正驱动你的，

175
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:09,200
for me, personally, is the fire inside of winning football games and performing well,
对我个人来说，是赢下比赛、踢出好状态那股内心的火焰，

176
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:14,910
and if I perform well as a striker for both Norway and City, I should be scoring goals.
如果我作为前锋在挪威和曼城都发挥出色，那我本就该进球。

177
00:11:14,910 --> 00:11:20,990
In the Odyssey, every challenge is followed by another, waiting just beyond the horizon.
在《奥德赛》里，每一道挑战之后，总有另一道在地平线那头等待。

178
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:23,950
For Erling, the first match is behind him.
对埃尔林而言，首场比赛已成过去。

179
00:11:23,950 --> 00:11:28,430
The recovery begins, and so does the preparation for what comes next.
恢复开始了，对下一场的备战也随之展开。

180
00:11:28,430 --> 00:11:31,150
We know each other for the last three years.
我们认识彼此已有三年。

181
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:33,230
We know what to do.
我们知道该怎么做。

182
00:11:33,230 --> 00:11:37,710
He's used to this kind of stage, this kind of pressure.
他习惯了这样的舞台、这样的压力。

183
00:11:37,710 --> 00:11:43,230
We just stay on top of it, and we carry on with the same job and procedures.
我们只要掌控好局面，照着同样的工作和流程继续做下去。

184
00:11:43,230 --> 00:11:46,670
So that's why Mario is with the national team.
所以马里奥才会跟着国家队。

185
00:11:46,670 --> 00:11:52,510
He's Italian, so he has a bit mixed feelings of being in the World Cup here now with Norway.
他是意大利人，所以如今跟着挪威征战世界杯，心情有点复杂。

186
00:11:52,510 --> 00:11:53,510
He's teasing, yeah?
他在打趣，对吧？

187
00:11:53,510 --> 00:12:00,350
Yeah, he's just scored a few goals against my own nation, but I can forgive it.
对啊，他刚在我祖国头上进了好几个球，不过我可以原谅他。

188
00:12:00,350 --> 00:12:04,190
I think we can do better and we've been working on it now in training,
我觉得我们能做得更好，现在训练里我们一直在打磨，

189
00:12:04,190 --> 00:12:10,830
try to get the performance even higher, because when we meet Senegal now, which is really good.
想把表现再提升一个档次，因为接下来要碰塞内加尔，他们真的很强。

190
00:12:10,830 --> 00:12:12,390
Again, we need to play at our best.
同样，我们得拿出最佳状态。

191
00:12:12,390 --> 00:12:13,360
We're at the World Cup.
我们身处世界杯。

192
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:15,230
So there's nothing to leave behind.
所以没有什么好保留的。

193
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:20,910
You need to show everything you can do, and you need to perform at your best in every single game.
你得展现自己的全部本事，每一场都拿出最好的表现。

194
00:12:20,910 --> 00:12:23,550
Every match tells its own story.
每一场比赛，都有属于它自己的故事。

195
00:12:23,550 --> 00:12:25,870
Time for reflection is over.
回味的时间结束了。

196
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:28,030
Another opponent awaits.
下一个对手已在等待。

197
00:12:28,030 --> 00:12:30,670
Another opportunity lies ahead.
又一个机会就在前方。

198
00:12:30,670 --> 00:12:35,670
This is Erling Haaland's road to the Cup, presented by Christopher Nolan's The Odyssey, in theaters July 17th.
这是埃尔林·哈兰德的世界杯之路，由克里斯托弗·诺兰的《奥德赛》呈现，7 月 17 日登陆影院。
